      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing AWS Secrets Manager**\n\nI've decided to move forward with AWS Secrets Manager as the external provider. Now, my focus is on how to integrate it cleanly into the `parse_json_secret.py` script. The code needs to be identifiable.\n\n\n**Defining Secret Retrieval**\n\nI'm now deep diving into how to structure the `parse_json_secret.py` file. I'm leaning heavily towards AWS Secrets Manager, specifically using the `boto3` library for the integration. My current thought is to ensure the code can easily identify itself as using this provider, likely through configuration or explicit identifiers within the script. The retrieval process itself seems straightforward, assuming a JSON format for the secret.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818272161,
          "start": 1789818269504
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b97b6f40001PyJ82cp6Yk0mKa",
      "message_id": "msg_0b97b6a5b001LmyN9Gam7jqfK8",
      "session_id": "ses_f468495b9ffe6fWLnWn0ensmN3",
